cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below and cite the accompanying article."
title: "CTCs-mechanics: multi-compartment finite-element model of the entry of circulating tumour cells into constrictions"
abstract: >-
  Code and data accompanying the manuscript "Cortical resistance and entry geometry govern the entry
  pressure of circulating tumour cells". Axisymmetric finite-strain multi-compartment cell model
  (Skalak cortex, near-incompressible neo-Hookean cytoplasm, nuclear envelope and nucleoplasm), the
  corrected reduction to critical entry pressure, the global sensitivity analysis, a reproducible
  population and device pipeline, and an interactive web app.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/Danpc11/CTCs-mechanics"
keywords: [circulating tumour cells, cell mechanics, finite element, microfluidics, cortex]
